"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With Qiskit Serverless, you can manage compute and data across your [Qiskit "
"pattern](/guides/intro-to-patterns), including CPUs, QPUs, and other compute"
" accelerators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamit ang Qiskit Serverless, maaari mong pamahalaan ang compute at data sa "
"buong [Qiskit pattern](/guides/intro-to-patterns) mo, kasama na ang mga CPU,"
" QPU, at iba pang compute accelerators.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set detailed statuses {#set-detailed-statuses}"
msgstr "Magtakda ng detalyadong mga status {#set-detailed-statuses}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Serverless workloads have several stages across a workflow. By default, the "
"following statuses are viewable with `job.status()`:\n"
msgstr ""
"Maraming yugto ang mga serverless workload sa isang workflow. Sa default, "
"ang mga sumusunod na status ay makikita gamit ang `job.status()`:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**`QUEUED`**: the workload is queued for classical resources\n"
msgstr ""
"**`QUEUED`**: ang workload ay nakapila para sa mga classical resources\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**`INITIALIZING`**: the workload is set up\n"
msgstr "**`INITIALIZING`**: ini-set up ang workload\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`RUNNING`**: the workload is currently running on classical resources\n"
msgstr ""
"**`RUNNING`**: kasalukuyang tumatakbo ang workload sa mga classical "
"resources\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**`DONE`**: the workload has successfully completed\n"
msgstr "**`DONE`**: matagumpay na natapos ang workload\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can also set custom statuses that further describe the specific workflow"
" stage, as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari ka ring magtakda ng mga custom na status na nagbibigay ng mas "
"detalyadong paglalarawan sa partikular na yugto ng workflow, tulad ng "
"sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"If you're reading the code cells locally in a notebook, you will see the `%%writefile` [magic command](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile). Executing cells with this magic command saves them to disk rather than executing them.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"If you're reading the code cells locally in a notebook, you will see the `%%writefile` [magic command](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile). Executing cells with this magic command saves them to disk rather than executing them.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After successful completion of this workload (with `save_result()`), this "
"status will be updated to `DONE` automatically.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos matagumpay na makumpleto ang workload na ito (gamit ang "
"`save_result()`), awtomatikong ia-update ang status na ito sa `DONE`.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Parallel workflows {#parallel-workflows}"
msgstr "Mga parallel na workflow {#parallel-workflows}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For classical tasks that can be parallelized, use the `@distribute_task` "
"decorator to define compute requirements needed to perform a task. Start by "
"recalling the `transpile_remote.py` example from the [Write your first "
"Qiskit Serverless program](/guides/serverless-first-program) topic with the "
"following code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa mga classical na gawain na maaaring i-parallelize, gamitin ang "
"`@distribute_task` decorator para tukuyin ang mga kinakailangang compute na "
"kailangan para maisagawa ang isang gawain. Simulan sa pag-alala sa halimbawa"
" ng `transpile_remote.py` mula sa paksa ng [Isulat ang iyong unang Qiskit "
"Serverless na programa](/guides/serverless-first-program) gamit ang "
"sumusunod na code.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following code requires that you have already [saved your "
"credentials](/guides/cloud-setup).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang sumusunod na code ay nangangailangan na [na-save mo na ang iyong mga "
"credentials](/guides/cloud-setup).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this example, you decorated the `transpile_remote()` function with "
"`@distribute_task(target={\"cpu\": 1})`. When run, this creates an "
"asynchronous parallel worker task with a single CPU core, and returns with a"
" reference to track the worker. To fetch the result, pass the reference to "
"the `get()` function. We can use this to run multiple parallel tasks:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa halimbawang ito, dinekorahan mo ang function na `transpile_remote()` ng "
"`@distribute_task(target={\"cpu\": 1})`. Kapag pinatakbo, lumilikha ito ng "
"asynchronous na parallel worker task na may iisang CPU core, at nagbabalik "
"ng reference para subaybayan ang worker. Para makuha ang resulta, ipasa ang "
"reference sa function na `get()`. Magagamit natin ito para magpatakbo ng "
"maraming parallel na gawain:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Explore different task configurations {#explore-different-task-"
"configurations}"
msgstr ""
"I-explore ang iba't ibang configuration ng gawain {#explore-different-task-"
"configurations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can flexibly allocate CPU, GPU, and memory for your tasks via "
"`@distribute_task()`. For Qiskit Serverless on IBM Quantum&reg; Platform, "
"each program is equipped with 16 CPU cores and 32 GB RAM, which can be "
"allocated dynamically as needed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari kang mag-allocate ng CPU, GPU, at memory para sa iyong mga gawain "
"nang flexible gamit ang `@distribute_task()`. Para sa Qiskit Serverless sa "
"IBM Quantum&reg; Platform, ang bawat programa ay may kasamang 16 CPU cores "
"at 32 GB RAM, na maaaring i-allocate nang dynamic ayon sa pangangailangan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"CPU cores can be allocated as full CPU cores, or even fractional "
"allocations, as shown in the following.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga CPU core ay maaaring i-allocate bilang buong CPU cores, o kahit "
"fractional na allocation, tulad ng ipinapakita sa sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Memory is allocated in number of bytes. Recall that there are 1024 bytes in "
"a kilobyte, 1024 kilobytes in a megabyte, and 1024 megabytes in a gigabyte. "
"To allocate 2 GB of memory for your worker, you need to allocate `\"mem\": 2"
" * 1024 * 1024 * 1024`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang memory ay ini-allocate sa bilang ng bytes. Tandaan na mayroon 1024 bytes"
" sa isang kilobyte, 1024 kilobytes sa isang megabyte, at 1024 megabytes sa "
"isang gigabyte. Para mag-allocate ng 2 GB ng memory para sa iyong worker, "
"kailangan mong mag-allocate ng `\"mem\": 2 * 1024 * 1024 * 1024`.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Manage data across your program {#manage-data-across-your-program}"
msgstr ""
"Pamahalaan ang data sa buong programa mo {#manage-data-across-your-program}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qiskit Serverless allows you to manage files in the `/data` directory across"
" all your programs. This includes several limitations:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pinapayagan ka ng Qiskit Serverless na pamahalaan ang mga file sa direktoryo"
" ng `/data` sa lahat ng iyong programa. Kasama dito ang ilang mga "
"limitasyon:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Only `tar` and `h5` files are supported today\n"
msgstr "Ang `tar` at `h5` na mga file lamang ang sinusuportahan sa ngayon\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is only a flat `/data` storage, and cannot have `/data/folder/` "
"subdirectories\n"
msgstr ""
"Flat na `/data` storage lamang ito, at hindi maaaring magkaroon ng "
"`/data/folder/` na mga subdirectory\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following shows how to upload files. Be sure you have authenticated to "
"Qiskit Serverless with your IBM Quantum account (see [Upload to Qiskit "
"Serverless](/guides/serverless-first-program#upload-to-qiskit-serverless) "
"for instructions).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang sumusunod ay nagpapakita kung paano mag-upload ng mga file. Tiyaking na-"
"authenticate ka na sa Qiskit Serverless gamit ang iyong IBM Quantum account "
"(tingnan ang [I-upload sa Qiskit Serverless](/guides/serverless-first-"
"program#upload-to-qiskit-serverless) para sa mga tagubilin).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, you can list all the files in your `data` directory. This data is "
"accessible to all programs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, maaari mong ilista ang lahat ng mga file sa iyong direktoryo ng "
"`data`. Ang data na ito ay accessible sa lahat ng programa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This can be done from a program by using `file_download()` to download the "
"file to the program environment, and uncompressing the `tar`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari itong gawin mula sa isang programa sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng "
"`file_download()` para i-download ang file sa kapaligiran ng programa, at "
"pag-uncompress ng `tar`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point, your program can interact with the files, as you would a "
"local experiment. `file_upload()` , `file_download()`, and `file_delete()` "
"can be called from your local experiment, or your uploaded program, for "
"consistent and flexible data management.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa puntong ito, maaari nang makipag-ugnayan ang iyong programa sa mga file, "
"tulad ng sa isang lokal na eksperimento. Ang `file_upload()`, "
"`file_download()`, at `file_delete()` ay maaaring tawagan mula sa iyong "
"lokal na eksperimento, o ang iyong na-upload na programa, para sa pare-"
"pareho at flexible na pamamahala ng data.\n"

